<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tobago</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tobago is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a> island north-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trinidad">Trinidad</a>, with which it forms the Republic of Trinidad and Tobago. In the 17th and 18th centuries it was contested by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a>, Courlanders, English, French and Spanish and changed hands many times. It was ceded to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> in 1763 and, after periods of French rule, finally in 1814, becoming a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> colony that was joined to Trinidad in 1889.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tobago.jpg" alt="Tobago" width="320" height="344" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CIA · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Td-map.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
